> > >>
> > >> There are always 2^T states where T is the number of primary periods. In
> > >> your code you specified 36 primary periods which is 2^36 = something like
> > >> 6.8 x 10^10 possible states. R can't handle this. This implies there is a
> > >> practical upper limit to the number of primary periods goccu can handle
> > >> (much like there is a practical limit to the number of species occuMulti
> > >> can handle).
